            {
                "entry_id": "f29bf729-bd69-321b-9456-2e32b3e1802d",
                "word": "Bismillah",
                "pos": "intj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5aa49ed0-0226-3725-88ac-ec14565e8eda",
                        "entry_id": "f29bf729-bd69-321b-9456-2e32b3e1802d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In the name of Allah! Used in belief of blessing the speaker's imminent action, especially prior to eating and drinking; sometimes used as an apotropaic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b73519b4-5fa6-4683-9a29-7dbb51b1081a",
                                "sense_id": "5aa49ed0-0226-3725-88ac-ec14565e8eda",
                                "text": "‘Bismillah!’ he exclaimed. ‘I call all here to witness that Rashîd, the son of Ali, called the Fair, is free henceforth to go what way he chooses.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6ba359d-6c17-4e5f-bf76-7b89520eee92",
                                "sense_id": "5aa49ed0-0226-3725-88ac-ec14565e8eda",
                                "text": "Thus recitation of Bismillah creates a sort of firm conviction in the existence of Allah, and also develops the sense of gratitude, in the mind of the servant of Allah, for all that Allah has provided for him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96979af4-e05e-4314-a6f1-848735ba9290",
                                "sense_id": "5aa49ed0-0226-3725-88ac-ec14565e8eda",
                                "text": "On the night before his execution he calls God in Arabic - \"Bismillah\" - and so regains his soul from Satan."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "12dc295b-4d23-3a2e-993f-70b56768f982",
                        "entry_id": "f29bf729-bd69-321b-9456-2e32b3e1802d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The basmala; the phrase Bismillahi ar-Rahmani ar-Rahim (“in the name of God, the Merciful, the Compassionate”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b13df6d6-ec85-46a4-92ec-5e6c324915cd",
                                "sense_id": "12dc295b-4d23-3a2e-993f-70b56768f982",
                                "text": "In Bismillah, Allah has chosen to mention only two of His attributes, Rahman and Rahim, out of all His numerous attributes and the verse does not mention any other Divine attribute;..."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
